  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "text": "PLEASE add the option to size all previews in the grid-based gallery view the same size. I do NOT want any of my photos randomly 4 times the size of the others using up 4 spots on the screen it makes it really jarring to scroll through searching for a particular photo.",
      "source": "Google Play Store",
      "source_id": "bfb0d9d2-17f9-416a-83ab-abe1255ae5b6",
      "date": "2026-09-03",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "endless_scrolling_fatigue"
      ],
      "segment": "gen_x"
    },
    {
      "text": "The photos aren't lost, they are 6 yr old photos that are present in the Google Photos Cloud. I restored them to a phone so I may edit them and use them. Restored images are sitting on their original calendar dates instead of the top. How can you expect anyone using a photo editing app or other app to spend time scrolling through 2026 to 2020 images when they have a lot of images? It never used to be like this. Your links are not relevant to the issue. Something changed on the backend. Thanks",
      "source": "Google Play Store",
      "source_id": "b83d8437-28ca-4f9d-a453-36dd41556022",
      "date": "2026-09-07",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "endless_scrolling_fatigue"
      ],
      "segment": "gen_x"
    },
    {
      "text": "Videos are bugging in my timeline. From a week ago till now, I can't search my backed up videos on Google Photos because as I scroll down my timeline, newer videos appear on wrong dates. This issue doesn't happen on desktop enviroment. I cleared my cache and did a reset on the app, but I'm sure this is a server-side problem. submitted by /u/Nusirra [link] [comments]",
      "source": "Reddit",
      "source_id": "reddit_t3_1fqsvox",
      "date": "2024-09-27",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "timeline_navigation_clunky"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    },
    {
      "text": "Review I really enjoy using Google Photos. It makes it easy to keep my pictures organized, find older memories, and have my photos backed up in one place. I especially like being able to search for photos without scrolling through thousands of pictures. The memories feature is also a nice touch because it brings back photos I may have forgotten about. Overall, Google Photos is convenient, easy to use, and a great way to keep important memories safe and organized. star star star star star",
      "source": "Apple App Store",
      "source_id": "appstore_14441051361",
      "date": "2026-08-17",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "endless_scrolling_fatigue"
      ],
      "segment": "gen_x"
    },
    {
      "text": "/u/Collectibl3 on What will be actually deleting? Scroll through your photo timeline. Anything with a cloud on the bottom right corner means it has been uploaded to the cloud. That's what's getting deleted!",
      "source": "Reddit",
      "source_id": "reddit_t1_mc9katf",
      "date": "2025-02-11",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "timeline_navigation_clunky"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    }
  ],
